      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-14797",
      ":question/problem": "The points $A$, $B$ and $C$ form a triangle. The points $A$ and $B$ are $4m$ apart, while the points $A$ and $C$ are $6m$ apart. The measure of the angle formed at the point $B$ is $40^{\u2218}$. Given that the angle formed at $C$ is an acute angle, what is its measure? **Round** the answer to **$2$ decimal places**.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
